  "rationale": "Only iterative and unrolled_k are available to me. The spec's hard constraints are throughput_msps>=32, max_abs_err<=2^-12, and sys_p99_batch_us<=0.5 (32 results within 0.5us of a 1us tick). Accuracy is family-independent and depends only on data_width/n_iter/guards/rounding, so I bound those to the region that can plausibly hit 2^-12 (data_width 14-20, n_iter 12-16, low guards) and let the exact model confirm. The real differentiator is throughput: iterative gives Fmax/32 Msps (needs very high Fmax), while unrolled_k gives k*Fmax/32 Msps (k=2..4 needs much lower Fmax). I split the budget evenly to map both fronts: iterative for the area-minimum corner, unrolled_k for the throughput-feasible corner. The batch-latency constraint (32 results in 0.5us) is tight for iterative (32 results x (N+3) cycles) but unrolled_k's k-way throughput and shorter per-result latency make it more likely to satisfy it; the cost model will report which designs actually pass. If neither family can meet throughput, I will report infeasible rather than settle for a violating design."
